WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know one thing you do
in your down time,

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.769 line:92%
which was very sweet of you.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
Last time you were here,
my son Axel had just been born

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you knitted
this wonderful hat for him

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:08.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-That is just incredible.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:12.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was --
His noggin is so big.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.781
It, like, basically fit hi
for like a day and a half.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was so warm.
But I am glad that you found

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
other people to make
your beautiful hats for.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is your cat, yeah?
-That is my cat.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.591 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:27.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
Coco. She --
I forced the hat upon her.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:31.865
-I'm very surprised --
I mean, Coco seems okay with it,

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:34.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I'm shocked that a cat
would be okay with this.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, she's tolerant.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I feel like
that's her general personality

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Isn't that -- Yeah,
that's the height of any cat

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the highest grade.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's five stars for a cat
is tolerance.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.545 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-You know, I'll take it.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:49.416
-Last time you were here,
you were doing "Deadpool."

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were talking
about the fact that being

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a comic-book movie
was very --

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of credit, a lot of
cachet, I should say, with -

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.258
You have German cousins.
You have a younger brother

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now you're
in the "Joker" movie.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:01.461 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Is it helping again?

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.963 size:84% position:42%
Is this even giving you
more cred with them?

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.932 line:92%
-Um, absolutely. I think -

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just recently saw my cousins
in Germany,

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:12.439
and they wanted me to sign stuff
and blah, blah, blah.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:15.108
And I'm, like "I'm your family."
-Yeah.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.242 line:92%
-Um, but, no. It's great.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.546
I think the familial validation,
you know, it matters most.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, absolutely.
-I'm glad to have it.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:25.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is funny. I'm realizing no
not one of my cousins

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.753 line:92%
has ever asked for my autograph.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-I'm kind of heartbroken.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also thought it was weird.
Nothing.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not your tears, your blood.
Nothing?

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:35.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nothing. You --
It's a beautifully acted film.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously,
you're fantastic in it.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
Joaquin Phoenix
is transformative.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:46.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
His body is -- I'm happy
you did not have to do that.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I read he ate
an apple a day.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Was that then weird

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you had sort of
a lunch break for everybod

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:54.848 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that you were --

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.950
You guys were eating human meals
and he was --

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He usually disappeared
during lunch,

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:02.422
but on set we always have
something called Crafty,

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is just food available
for everyone else

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.893 size:78% position:39%
because you're around
for 12 hours a day.

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:10.363 line:92%
And I was pretty unabashedly

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of eating my way
through the day.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he would
sometimes cheat, too,

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.237 line:92%
and have like three pretzels

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Then run off.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:21.040
-There was a scene
where he looked a little flabby,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I thought
that was probably pretzel day.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:24.811 line:92%
-That was pretzel day for sure

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:27.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Then the Joker got real chubb
in this one scene.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:29.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
You also worked
with Natalie Portman

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.418
in a film that's coming ou
called "Lucy in the Sky."

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is based on a true stor
about astronauts.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you got to be an astronaut.
-Yeah, I did. Yes.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.959
-Did you enjoy putting on
the astronaut costume?

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that something
that you found exciting?

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:46.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think what's nice
about being an actor is, like,

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.302
I feel, like there are all these
career doors that have close

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
for me, like being an athlet
or an astronaut.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:57.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's really fun
to kind of put on somethin

00:02:57.243 --> 00:03:00.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be, like "Oh, yeah.
I have the cred

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
the intelligence to be here.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.385 line:92%
But it is fun to play in that,

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:08.955
and that is something that
like, draws me to performing

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:12.091
is I get to play all these
other versions of myself.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's true,
because the other path

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:18.531
to wearing an astronaut outfit
is like 20 years of training

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like.
-Yeah.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:22.101
-And for you to just get cast,
I mean, you really cut the line.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know. Yeah.
-And then "Atlanta."

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys are going
back to work there.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:28.474 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Is that exciting?

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I'm really
looking forward to that.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:31.377 line:92%
I think that show, to me,

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:35.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
feels so much like a homecomin
or like a family thing,

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, in a way
'cause we all really

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
found footing in our careers
on that show

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
and feel sort of like
this safe place,

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:45.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so, you know,
I'm really looking forward

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:46.826 line:92%
to going back and doing that

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How long of a break
will it have been

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
between the last time
you guys were on set together?

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:56.002
-My God. We were on set together
end of 2017.

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow. Really?
-So almost -- almost two years

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really great,
and it's nice --

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:02.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I feel, like that show
is in such safe hands

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:03.676 size:78% position:39% line:92%
based on the quality,

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.345 size:81% position:41%
the level of quality
and consistency of it,

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.913 size:84% position:42%
so it's nice to know
that it will come back.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think there are sometime
shows where you worry

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:11.484
about a layoff, and that's one
where I have no worries at all

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:15.855
-Ah, thank you. We have a lovely
group chat going on, so...

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:18.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, you know,
the energy is still there

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:19.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everybody
is excited to go back.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:22.328
-That's great. Well, it's always
so lovely to have you here

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:26.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations on everything.
Zazie Beetz, everybody.

